  ]
}
```

This DSM represents the interactions as follows:
- Diagonal elements are all 1 since each component interacts with itself.
- The Bit directly interacts with the Transmission and is housed by the Housing, thus [1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0].
- The Transmission directly interacts with the Bit, Motor, and is housed by the Housing, thus [1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 0].
- The Motor directly interacts with the Transmission, Electrical System, and is housed by the Housing, thus [0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1, 0].
- The Electrical System directly interacts with the Motor, Battery Holder, and all are housed by the Housing, thus [0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0].
- The Battery Holder directly interacts with the Electrical System and is housed by the Housing, thus [0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0].
- The Housing physically encloses all components (Bit, Transmission, Motor, Electrical System, Battery Holder) and interacts with the External Environment, thus [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1].
- The External Environment directly interacts with the Housing, thus [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1].

This analysis simplifies complex interactions into a binary format for clarity and focuses on direct physical or functional dependencies.
